      ],
      "title": "Senate adjourned (Senate Daily Press Gallery log)",
      "official_text": "3:50 p.m. The Senate adjourned and will reconvene at 3:00 p.m. on Monday, August 4. At 5:30 p.m. they will vote on the motion to invoke cloture on the motion to proceed to H.R. 6500-Legislative vehicle for Continuing Resolution. Senator Thune filed cloture on the motion to proceed to H.R. 6500-legislative vehicle for Continuing Resolution. The following resolutions were agreed to en bloc: S. Res. 821-National Whistleblower Appreciation Day S. Res. 822-American grown flowers and foliage S. Res. 823-National Farmer’s Market week S. Res. 824-Gold Star Children’s Day S. Res. 825-Mississippi Christian University bicentennial The following military promotions were agreed to en bloc: Cal. #s 877-880 Cal. #s 882-892 Cal. #s 894-898 Cal. #881, with the exception of Stephen P. Snelson All nominations on the Secretary’s Desk in the Air Force, Army, Navy, and Space Force with the exception of PN835-2, PN925, PN970-2, PN1151 Omar Vargas, PN1015-2, PN1017-2, PN1061-2, PN1065-2, PN1072-2, PN1104 Austin D. Roberts and John A. Goodwin, PN1105 Justin M. Smith, PN990-2, and PN1029-2.",
      "importance": {
        "tier": "P2",
